A||||7||CUTTER||fieroGT    Vs.     91 Camaro 305 V8||||1||
Z||000000||CUTTER||04-24-2000||02:50 AM||||about 2 weeks ago I got my 8mm accell wires and figured I go test um out, well I did feel my lost horsepower comeback and wanted to race this kid at school who has a 91 camaro 305ci V8 for about a month now. I went to the local hangout the Ephrata Cloister aka "the strip" and seen him sitting there in the lot. So I asked him if he wanted to race he said "umm.....I guess" so we hit the light when it turned green we both nailed it "both automatics" and I had him till about 55-65 then I seen his front nose inching....I mean INCHING past me. By about 100 he won about a car length. I thought this V8 camaro "1991" would be a little faster then this....or either my car is a little faster then I think! I am the 3rd owner and I dint realize in any aftermarket mods when I bought it except fot the holly scoop. How do I find out if my car has aftermarket performance?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||04-24-2000||03:01 AM||||.<p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 04-24-2000).]||||reg||14
Z||000002||sid1200||04-24-2000||03:25 AM||||keep in mind the 305 RS which is what I assume he has is only a 170hp/255 torque engine, which should be faster then a fiero AT stock ,but not by all that much, and much depends on the take off and the individual car involved.<BR>a 305 Z28 is a different story, the RS doesnt' have TPI injection...||||reg||1
Z||000003||pollock||04-24-2000||12:33 PM||||A year or two ago, some little punkass pulled up next to me in a new (96/7 or so) Z28.  Couldn't have been older than 16.  Had his little girlie ridin' shotgun.  I have a really crappy looking 86 GT.  4 spd.  <P>So his girl looks over and laughs at my car.  I revved at him, and we went at it.  I swear to all of you that i blasted him by 6 car lengths, easy.  He didn't catch me till i hit 3rd gear (he was doubling my speed at that point).  <P>My buddy was behind me in his Suburban.  Glad i had a witness, for bench racing sessions like these.<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000004||Sleeper||04-24-2000||12:42 PM||||That Z28 should have smoked you man, he probably didn't have the balls to race and you embarassed him in front of his girl, ha ha.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cooter||04-24-2000||06:13 PM||||You can usually catch those guys with their "superiority complex" sleeping at the light. If they think your car is a real dog, they won't put much effort into racing you. I live in a college town, so these young folks get a new car and away from mommy and daddy think they are king of the world. Some punks in a Mitsub. 3000GT laughed at my Civic. Same scenerio: I watched the turning lanes go to caution, reved the poor little econobox and launched a split second before the light changed to green. It took him about 3 full blocks to catch up. Then I looked at him and laughed out while pointing at their new car. I yelled to them that if he could not out run a Civic in a "real" car, he should go back home.||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||04-24-2000||11:12 PM||||I've won and lost races at the launch. A Fiero has a good deal of torque for a small car. Make good use of it at the start. Even if the joker catches you on top end, he just might have more respect for a Fiero next time round.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Shaun41178||04-26-2000||12:46 AM||||Nice try with that Bird Cutter.  Get a pulley, port the exhaust manifolds, and a shift kit and you should be able to take that bird the whole way.<P>I raced my freinds TBI 305 170 hp bird before  I had any mods on my car(85 Gt auto)  He only got one car on me up to 80 and half that carlength was his extra torque getting me off the line.<P>With a pulley you should pick up about .1-.2 or so in the qtr which is about half a car or so and the other mods like exhaust will give a bit more better breathing in the upper rpms.  Do those mods and race again and i can be almost 100% certain that he won't pass you next time.<P>Shaun||||reg||1
